---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE, SOCIAL } from '../data/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Jajati AI"
  description="Jajati AI makes the AI Explained series: practical AI, better prompts and AI concepts explained in simple Hindi, on Instagram and YouTube."
  breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'About' }]}
  pageType="about"
>
  <article class="container-ja max-w-3xl pt-6 md:pt-10">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold md:text-5xl">About Jajati AI</h1>
    <div class="prose-ja mt-6">
      <p class="text-lg">{SITE.positioning}</p>
      <p>
        Jajati AI is a creator project. It makes <strong>AI Explained</strong>, a series of short videos in Hinglish on
        <a href={SOCIAL.instagram.url} rel="noopener">Instagram ({SOCIAL.instagram.handle})</a> and
        <a href={SOCIAL.youtube.url} rel="noopener">YouTube ({SOCIAL.youtube.handle})</a>. Each episode explains one AI
        idea (tokens, context windows, hallucinations, RAG, prompt engineering) and ends with something you can try the
        same day.
      </p>
      <h2>Why this website exists</h2>
      <p>
        People comment a keyword on a reel to get a prompt sheet. Instagram does not always let those messages through,
        so this site is the reliable place for every free resource: open it, copy the prompt, download the sheet. No
        login, no DM, no follow needed.
      </p>
      <h2>How the content is made</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Prompts come from the published cheat sheets and video scripts. Each prompt page says where it comes from.</li>
        <li>Facts in the lessons are checked against the sources listed at the end of each episode.</li>
        <li>Example outputs are only shown when they are real. Nothing here is an invented test result.</li>
        <li>The videos use an AI voice-over and are labelled as AI content on Instagram and YouTube.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Independent</h2>
      <p>
        Jajati AI is not affiliated with OpenAI, Google, Anthropic or any other AI company. Product names are used only
        to say which tool a prompt is meant for.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
